+### §viewport-not-container — the shell's layout step follows the viewport
+- Since: 2026-10-22
+- Decision: the shell's layout step uses a viewport `@media (min-width: 720px)` query. `.shell` is no longer a query
+  container (`container-type` removed).
+- Supersedes: §container-not-viewport (2026-09-15), which required `@container` queries on `.shell` and forbade
+  viewport `@media` width queries.
+- Reason: maintainer override (2026-10-22).
+- Known trade-off: the shell renders inside split panes as narrow as 380px on a 1440px screen; with a viewport query
+  such a pane gets the two-column layout, which clipped the sidebar in the 2026-09-14 incident.
